  "description": "The whole file is read successfully and then 9000-CARDFILE-CLOSE fails. The close paragraph at app/cbl/CBACT02C.cbl:136-152 spells its arithmetic with ADD and SUBTRACT where the open uses MOVE - ADD 8 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT at :137, SUBTRACT APPL-RESULT FROM APPL-RESULT at :140, ADD 12 TO ZERO GIVING APPL-RESULT at :142 - and the effects are identical to MOVE 8, MOVE 0 and MOVE 12. Here the CLOSE reports the '9' permanent-error status, so :139 takes its ELSE, APPL-RESULT becomes 12, and the error arm at :147-150 emits 'ERROR CLOSING CARDFILE', the image '9000' and 'ABENDING PROGRAM'. The decisive expectation is the absence of the end banner: :85 sits after PERFORM 9000-CARDFILE-CLOSE at :83, so a failing close means the program never announces that it finished. Fifty-four lines out - one banner, fifty records, three error lines - and RETURN-CODE 12.",
